{
 "id": "pioneer_ddj_400_midi",
 "name": "Pioneer DDJ-400",
 "protocol": "midi",
 "about": "The DDJ-400 as it comes, USB MIDI class (no driver). Each deck on its own channel (1, 2), its pads on 8 and 10 (9 and 11 with SHIFT), the mixer and the browser on 7, Beat FX on 5. SHIFT is the controller's own: held, its buttons send other notes, which this layout names as the same controls. Knobs and faders are 14-bit (MSB, then LSB), the jogs count from 0x40, 720 ticks a turn; the platter touched sends on one CC, its side on another. Lights: the button's own note, 0x7F/0x00; the level meters CC 0x02 on the deck's channel; a deck's jog ring flashes on note n of channel 16 when a record is loaded. From Mixxx's mapping by Warker, nschloe, dj3730, jusko and tiesjan.",
 "match": {
  "names": [
   "DDJ-400"
  ]
 },
