 "notes": {
  "deck.a.shift": "SHIFT: held, the other controls' second meanings.",
  "deck.a.jog.scratch": "The platter touched on top: the hard bend (as the RMX in SCRATCH). Its side, or spun untouched: the nudge. SHIFT + the platter: search.",
  "deck.a.pitch": "TEMPO, down is faster. SHIFT + BEAT SYNC cycles its range \u00b18 \u2192 16 \u2192 50 %.",
  "deck.a.trim": "TRIM: the deck's gain, \u00b112 dB.",
  "deck.a.filter": "CFX: the filter, low-pass left, high-pass right.",
  "deck.a.hotcue.1": "HOT CUE pads 1\u20138: set, then jump; SHIFT clears.",
  "deck.a.beatloop.1": "BEAT LOOP pads: \u00bc \u2192 32 beats from the bar; the same again lets go.",
  "deck.a.beatjump.1": "BEAT JUMP pads: 1, 2, 4, 8 beats back (odd) and on (even).",
  "show.hit": "SAMPLER pads are the show's: 1 the scene before, 2 the next, 3 a hit, 4 blackout, 5 freeze, 6 strobe while held.",
  "deck.a.loop.in": "LOOP IN / OUT / RELOOP-EXIT; SHIFT + IN a 4-beat loop; CUE/LOOP CALL \u25c0 \u25b6 halve and double it, with SHIFT jump 32 beats.",
  "deck.a.pfl": "CUE (headphones): the deck in the headphones, before its fader \u2014 where the Desk has headphones (Settings \u2192 Sound: the DDJ's own 3/4 by itself). With one output, the show's: the scene before (A), the next (B). SHIFT: freeze (A), blackout (B).",
  "fx.on": "Beat FX is the echo: CH SELECT picks the deck (MASTER: both), LEVEL/DEPTH its send, ON/OFF on and off.",
  "mixer.headMix": "HEADPHONES MIXING and LEVEL are the DDJ's own: it blends the master (its 1/2) and the cued decks (its 3/4) into the phones jack itself."
 }
}
